// Code generator: walks the checked AST and emits assembly through the
// target interface (target.tach), in terms of its virtual registers.
// Every expression leaves its value in the accumulator; operands wait on
// the stack of temporaries; locals live in frame slots.
//
// Calling convention: the platform's C convention for scalars (so
// functions can be passed to C, e.g. as qsort callbacks). Structs, tuples
// and arrays are passed as a pointer to a copy made by the caller, and
// returned through a result pointer (R_RESULT: x8 on AArch64, the hidden
// first argument rdi on x86-64).
//
// Labels: a loop node's `z` is its continue label; z + 1 is its break
// label (z + 2 the condition of a `for`).
//
// This file holds the program and function level: the driver
// (compile_program, every pass in order), static data, functions and
// their parameters, statements, and the frame slots and temporaries the
// parts share. The parts: expr.tach (expressions, operators, aggregates,
// assignment), control.tach (match and its patterns, if, loops),
// vector.tach (SIMD vectors, lane by lane), call.tach (calls and the
// argument-passing convention).

mod expr;
mod control;
mod vector;
mod call;

